spec.section:
### 9.5 Security across the boundary

- per-gateway auth: the harness holds one token per endpoint, resolved from a local secret store
  (never inside the config file itself); tokens are least-privileged for that host's role set;
- the director's grants travel with the message, not with the network: a supervisor on host D can
  do only what its role grant says, no matter which host asked it;
- no host learns the topology beyond its own endpoint: an agent's config view contains its own
  gateway and its DuckBrain keys, never the fleet map;
- the scheduler/registry endpoints on remote hosts are read-only to the harness unless that host's
  config grants otherwise.
